            <ArticleTitle>Septic sacroiliitis during the postpartal period. Diagnostic contribution of magnetic resonance imaging.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>512-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Septic sacroiliitis is an uncommon condition that is often diagnosed late. Two cases in the immediate postpartal period are reported. Magnetic resonance imaging contributed decisively to the early diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
